{"name":"Frivolous Folly","hex":"#cfd2c7","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frivolous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Silly, especially at an inappropriate time or in an inappropriate manner; lacking a good reason for being, or for doing what one does; due to or moved by a caprice or whim.","Of little weight or importance; not worth notice; slight; trivial."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frivolous"},{"term":"folly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Foolishness that results from a lack of foresight or lack of practicality.","Thoughtless action resulting in tragic consequence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To follow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/folly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Folly","blocks":[{"text":"In architecture, a folly is a building constructed primarily for decoration, but suggesting through its appearance some other purpose, or of such extravagant appearance that it transcends the range of usual garden buildings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Broadway_tower.jpg/330px-Broadway_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folly","wikidata":"Q180174"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Broadway_tower.jpg/500px-Broadway_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Broadway_tower.jpg/1280px-Broadway_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Broadway_tower.jpg/500px-Broadway_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Broadway Tower, Worcestershire, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABroadway_tower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com